      "writtenOn": "2022-02-01T16:03:38Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "To make this line up with how the rest of SkBitmapDevice configures SkDraws, can you change this to be:\n\n   if (!this-\u003eaccessPixels(\u0026draw.fDst)) {\n       return; // no pixels to draw to so skip it\n   }\n   \naccessPixels() is the gate that notifies that pixels are drawn (done in BDDraw or SkDrawTiler). Unfortunately neither of these helpers are applicable for drawSpecial, but the manual setting of the SkDraw missed this step!  If we do it this way, drawSpecial\u0027s access is handled the same way as every where else, and the l586 you added can be deleted then.",
